    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d175-a1">

                <pb facs="0221" n="161" sameAs="frus:frus1895p1/pg161"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in No. 2402—Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hixson to Mr. Denby</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-10-15"><hi rendition="#small-caps">October</hi> 15,
                            1895</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Forty-three convicted, of whom 7 executed; balance in viceroy’s hands several
                    weeks awaiting action; 139 under arrest, including convicted. Many not
                    incriminated now being released on security. Over 100 present at Huashan still
                    at large; 1, if not more, ringleader at large.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hixson</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
